fficial examples","Runnable source","Further reading",[90,91,92],{"_51":97,"_25":98},{"_51":95,"_25":96},{"_51":93,"_25":94},"Pinned package lock","https://github.com/Unity-Technologies/2d-techdemos/blob/6593d544df2ea598e51f5cf1d7165d5ed42ceba7/Packages/packages-lock.json#L27-L36","Pinned package manifest","https://github.com/Unity-Technologies/2d-techdemos/blob/6593d544df2ea598e51f5cf1d7165d5ed42ceba7/Packages/manifest.json#L2-L14","Pinned editor baseline","https://github.com/Unity-Technologies/2d-techdemos/blob/6593d544df2ea598e51f5cf1d7165d5ed42ceba7/ProjectSettings/ProjectVersion.txt#L1-L2","Project source",[101],{"_51":99,"_25":57},"Why it belongs here","Offers source scenes for tile collision lookup, destructible maps, and palette switching. The inspected project records Unity 6000.3.3f1, URP 17.3.0, and Input System 1.17.0, while the README says 2021.1 onward. Its manifest selects 2d-extras' package_6000.3 Git branch but the committed lockfile records registry 6.0.1; resolve and pin dependencies before testing. Source review did not establish import, playback, or compatibility across Editor versions.","detail","guidance","Resource type","Documentation","Category","Engines & creation tools","category","lead","summary","name","engines","docs",[56,74,85,86,87],[124,125,126,127],[123],[120,121,122],{"_51":97,"_25":98},{"_51":95,"_25":96},{"_51":93,"_25":94},"2d","code","assets","scene","test",{"_129":130},"documents",{"_131":132,"_133":134},"en",[136,140,141,142,139,143,144,145,146,147,148,149,150,151,152,153,154,155,156,157,158,159,160,161,162,163,164,165,166,167,168,169,170,171,172,173,174,138,175,137,176,177,178,179,180,181,182,183,184,185,186,187,188,189,190,191,192,193,194,195,196],"zh",[135,136,137,138,139],"reading-guide","practical-guide","level-design-skill","deployment","publishing-platforms","tutorials-and-demos","coding-agent-game-code","game-testing-library","agents-notes","engines-notes","game-ai-notes","cadle-repositories","world-model-notes","rese